    description: 'Focusrite Scarlett 2i2 Studio 4th Gen Recording Bundle Scarlett 2i2 Studio is everything you need to record your music to release-ready standards. Hook up the CM25 MkIII condenser microphone to our most detailed ultra-low-noise mic preamps. Plug guitars straight in to 2i2’s Hi-Z inputs. Connect keys and synths to the super-high-quality line ins. Then listen in detail with the SH-450 headphones. Auto Gain and Clip Safe make sure you’ll never need to worry about your levels. Air mode, with Presence and Harmonic Drive, gives you that big console sound wherever you record. And the Hitmaker Expansion software bundle includes all the tools you need to record, produce and release your tracks. Two of our most detailed, ultra-low-noise preamps. Plug into 2i2’s 4th-Generation remote-controlled preamps – Scarlett’s clearest and most detailed ever, with a huge 69dB gain range to get huge, dynamic sound, whatever you’re recording. CM25 MkIII studio condenser mic You can use the CM25 MkIII for almost anything, but you’ll love how it sounds on vocals and guitars thanks to its bright and detailed character. SH-450 closed-back headphones With the SH-450 we’ve created our best-sounding studio headphones, with plush pads and a soft-touch headband design to keep you focused, not fatigued. Two Hi-Z guitar inputs that feel just like an amp Hi-Z instrument inputs, just like you’d find on an amp, make guitars sound great for DI’s and amp sims Two super-high-quality line inputs capture all the character of your synths and keys Let 2i2 handle your levels. Auto Gain sets your levels and Clip Safe keeps them in the sweet spot, automatically tweaking the gain if you’re in danger of clipping. You’ll never lose a take again. Get big console sound with two re-engineered Air modes: Presence and all-new Harmonic Drive All the software you need to make a hit record. Once you’ve got started with Ableton Live Lite or three months of Pro Tools Artist recording software (both included), the Hitmaker Expansion bundle has everything you need to bring big studio sound to your songs, with an unbeatable range of record-making studio tools from the biggest names in the business. The choice of six million music makers Huge 120dB dynamic range for incredible recordings Scarlett delivers incredible audio quality, with converters direct from our flagship RedNet interfaces- as found in high-end studios around the world Loud and clear Our custom-designed headphone amp design sets the stage for the best playback you’ve ever heard from a Scarlett interface, driving high-impedance headphones louder and clearer than ever before Easy Start Need help getting set up? Just tell our Easy Start tool what you want to do and we’ll guide you through all the software and setup you need, with recording tips and other helpful content along the way. Three-year warranty Millions of musicians rely on Scarlett every day, and we make some of the more dependable interfaces in the business. However, should the unexpected happen, every Focusrite interface comes with three-year warranty – just in case. Award-winning, global support If you need help at any point you can reach out to our award-winning global support team. We work 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, 365 days a year, so you can too – if you want. Specifications in detail Overview Number of Microphone Preamps -2 Phantom Power -Yes Instrument Inputs -2 Line Inputs- 2 Air Mode -Yes Auto Gain -Yes Clip Safe- Yes Line Outputs -2 Headphone Outputs – 1 Loopback – Yes Connectivity -USB Type-C Protocol -USB 2.0 Form Factor -Desktop Simultaneous I/O4 x 2 (including Loopback inputs) A/D Resolution – 24-bit/192 kHz Bus Powered – Yes (900mA) Microphone – CM25 MKIII Condenser Headphones – SH-450 Closed-back XLR Cable – 3m Supported sample rates 44.1kHz, 48kHz, 88.2kHz, 96kHz, 176.4kHz, 192kHz Microphone inputs Frequency Response20-20kHz ± 0.06dB Dynamic Range116dB (A-Weighted) THD+N-100dB @ 8dB gain Noise EIN-127dBu (A-Weighted) Maximum Input Level16dBu Gain Range69dB Impedance3kΩ Line inputs Frequency Response20-20kHz ± 0.05dB Dynamic Range115.5dB (A-Weighted) THD+N-100dB @ 8dB gain Maximum Input Level22dBu Gain Range69dB Impedance60kΩ Instrument inputs Frequency Response20-20kHz ± 0.15dB Dynamic Range113dB (A-Weighted) THD+N-80dB @ minimum gain Maximum Input Level12dBu Gain Range62dB Impedance1MΩ Line outputs (Balanced) Frequency Response20-20kHz ± 0.02dB Dynamic Range120dB THD+N-109dB Maximum Output Level16dBu Impedance100Ω Headphone outputs Frequency Response20-20kHz ± 0.1dB @ 33Ω / 300Ω Dynamic Range112dB @ 33Ω 115dB @ 300Ω THD+N-99dB @ 33Ω -108dB @ 300Ω Maximum Output Level2.5dBu into 33Ω 10dBu into 300Ω Maximum Output Power32mW into 33Ω 22mW into 300Ω Impedance50Ω Analogue to Digital Converter THD+N-110dB Dynamic Range120dB Digital to Analogue Converter THD+N-115dB Dynamic Range130dB (A-Weighted) Power USB900mA External (Optional)4.5W',
