    id: 'yamaha-fc5-sustain-pedal',
    name: 'Yamaha FC5 Sustain Pedal',
    category: 'Keyboards',
    shortDescription: 'Yamaha FC5 Sustain Pedal For those electronic keyboards with an input jack labeled “SUSTAIN,” the FC5 is used in the same manner the sustain pedal on an acoustic piano is used....',
    description: 'Yamaha FC5 Sustain Pedal For those electronic keyboards with an input jack labeled “SUSTAIN,” the FC5 is used in the same manner the sustain pedal on an acoustic piano is used. A specially designed rubber bottom grips the floor and stays put while you play. The FC5 can also be utilized as an FS controller for synthesizers, tone modules and drum machines. Product Information FC5 Foot Switch Style Sustain Pedal Foot switch for sustain and other momentary (on/off) functions The colors and finishes shown may vary from those on the actual products. Yamaha FC5 Sustain Pedal The Yamaha FC5 is a popular sustain pedal designed for electronic keyboards and digital pianos. It is commonly used to sustain notes or chords, providing a more expressive and realistic playing experience for musicians. Here are some key features and information about the Yamaha FC5 Sustain Pedal: Functionality : The Yamaha FC5 is a simple and durable footswitch pedal that functions as a sustain pedal. When you press down on the pedal, it sustains the sound of the notes or chords you are playing on the keyboard until you release it. This functionality mimics the sustain effect of an acoustic piano, allowing for smoother transitions between notes and enhancing the overall musical performance. Compatibility : The FC5 sustain pedal is compatible with a wide range of Yamaha keyboards and digital pianos. Additionally, it can work with other keyboard brands that support a standard footswitch input (usually 1/4-inch jack) for sustain pedals. Always check the compatibility with your specific instrument before purchasing. Polarity Switch : The FC5 features a polarity switch on the back of the pedal. This switch allows you to reverse the pedal’s polarity if needed, ensuring compatibility with keyboards that have different sustain pedal behavior. Most Yamaha instruments will work with the default setting, but it’s a handy feature for ensuring proper functionality with other brands. Compact and Sturdy Design : The Yamaha FC5 is designed to be compact and lightweight, making it easy to carry around and use in different settings. Despite its size, it is built to be durable and withstand the demands of regular use. Versatility : While the main purpose of the FC5 is as a sustain pedal, some musicians use it for other functions as well. In some keyboards, the sustain pedal can be used for tasks like activating specific effects or triggering other features. Affordability : One of the advantages of the Yamaha FC5 sustain pedal is its affordability. It provides a cost-effective solution for adding sustain functionality to your keyboard setup without breaking the bank. Alternative Models : In addition to the FC5, Yamaha also offers other sustain pedal options, including the FC3A, FC4A, and FC7 models. Each model may have slight differences in features and build quality, so be sure to choose the one that best suits your needs and budget.',
